 </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T21:08:58-08:00","id":1502478,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat book was so bad I dropped V5 so yeah, I agree with that. Shame too because I thought Blood Gods was very solid and it was on the verge of getting me hooked into V5, which I had largely been uninterested in up until that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T00:47:09-08:00","id":1502486,"title":"","content":"This should have been out 5 years ago. But at least it's coming out. It's also got a degree of utilitarian use by compiling a lot of useful stuff in one place. I don't think I'll be getting it because it has nothing to offer me but i imagine it's a solid purchase for v5 players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T01:58:15-08:00","id":1502490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Welard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502476#post1502476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That cover... I long for the 90s, 2000s drawn covers. This feels like it was made by a Freshman photography student.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they want to emphasize LARP more in the Tabletop-side in the franchise. I too miss the 2000s drawn cover aesthetic of oWod, and I wish they'll just leave all the LARP themes in the actual spinoff MET stuff. The Live-Action stuff doesn't appeal to me at, personally. <br /> <br /> Also, I thought the V5 Players Guide was already released for free? Are they re-releasing it again, but this time it has a price-tag to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T02:09:14-08:00","id":1502492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502477#post1502477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Renegade sadly is just not meeting my high expectations as set by OPP. THE SABBAT and THE SECOND INQUISITION just weren't as good as BLOOD GODS or CHICAGO BY NIGHT.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it also seems to be the case that the OPP-books sold better because Renegade is doing a physical print rerun of Chicago By Night this year.<br /> <br /> As an aside, what I found strange about this, in particular, is that when this was announced during Renegadecon Onyx Path was never mentioned. Chicago By Night was just this V5 chronicle book that came out in the past and it may be hard to get your hands on physical copies of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T05:27:47-08:00","id":1502500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502492#post1502492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, what I found strange about this, in particular, is that when this was announced during Renegadecon Onyx Path was never mentioned. Chicago By Night was just this V5 chronicle book that came out in the past and it may be hard to get your hands on physical copies of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's easier for me to get a physical copy of CbN than the Second Inquisition book! Sure it would be PoD, but PoD isn't inherently bad.<br /> <br /> But yeah. This may be the book that makes V5 worthwhile, but I've already dropped \u00a3110 on V5 (of which about \u00a350 was worth it). I really don't want to spend another \u00a350 to complete it, especially as the game's still going to be incomplete (mostly due to no playable Sabbat). I'm also going to agree I'm not a fan of the cover, but I'm really not a big fan of the V5 art direction anyway (I like monochrome images and I hate that many RPGs avoid them).<br /> <br /> Also nonplayable Sabbat but playable Salubri? Are we going to get a write-up for the Seven again, despite most Salubri being either Sabbat or Ashirra? I really hope not, the Seven are by far the least interesting part of the Clan. I'll take any Salubri writeup over more Seven, even literally making them soul eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T05:52:42-08:00","id":1502502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502500#post1502500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also nonplayable Sabbat but playable Salubri? Are we going to get a write-up for the Seven again, despite most Salubri being either Sabbat or Ashirra? I really hope not, the Seven are by far the least interesting part of the Clan. I'll take any Salubri writeup over more Seven, even literally making them soul eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>They first got a write-up in the V5 Companion from 2020. There, the Seven, Golconda and Saulot are vaguely mentioned. Salubri had one of the worst Banes, though: other Vampires think their blood tastes great and that whenever Salubri use Disciplines their third Eye starts bleeding and said bleeding leads to other vampires nearby having to make Hunger Frenzy checks (if they have Hunger 4 or more).<br /> <br /> But with this new Player Guide they will get a new write-up and another option for a Bane, so Salubri is one of those Clans that will definitely benefit from this book.<br /> <br /> And who knows why from among the more obscure Clan/Bloodlines it was the Salubri they decided to make a playable option in V5...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T06:30:52-08:00","id":1502508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502490#post1502490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they want to emphasize LARP more in the Tabletop-side in the franchise. I too miss the 2000s drawn cover aesthetic of oWod, and I wish they'll just leave all the LARP themes in the actual spinoff MET stuff. The Live-Action stuff doesn't appeal to me at, personally.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought the V5 Players Guide was already released for free? Are they re-releasing it again, but this time it has a price-tag to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They could at least create some more interesting covers with their larpers. They are just so generic.<br /> <br /> The players guide was not released, no. This should be a pretty substantial shakeup for the game having all 13 clans and some new bane type stuff hinted. I'm sure we'll get additional predator types as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27749-welard","name":"Welard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T07:02:19-08:00","id":1502513,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest concern is the Clan depiction re-writes they mentioned. Matthew did a great job updating the clans across the spectrum. The only three clan write-ups he didn't do (Ravnos, Salubri and Tzimisce) feel to me as the least-connected to established lore. Achilli mentioned in a video that they started with the Verbs on these three and then built the Clans up to match the Verbs, including traits and new Discipline lineups. Rather than take the opportunity to course-correct the Clan depictions in the Companion to adhere to the lore of the previous 30 years of Clan development, I feel like they are going to re-write Matthew\u2019s current Clan write-ups to adhere more closely to Achilli's Verb list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T08:08:42-08:00","id":1502514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502513#post1502513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest concern is the Clan depiction re-writes they mentioned. Matthew did a great job updating the clans across the spectrum. The only three clan write-ups he didn't do (Ravnos, Salubri and Tzimisce) feel to me as the least-connected to established lore. Achilli mentioned in a video that they started with the Verbs on these three and then built the Clans up to match the Verbs, including traits and new Discipline lineups. Rather than take the opportunity to course-correct the Clan depictions in the Companion to adhere to the lore of the previous 30 years of Clan development, I feel like they are going to re-write Matthew\u2019s current Clan write-ups to adhere more closely to Achilli's Verb list.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lasombra one was a bit crap but it was always going to be tricky to build them into v5 do he was making a purse out of pig skin. I didn't think much of the setite one since it homogenised the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T11:36:10-08:00","id":1502527,"title":"","content":"I'm curious myself on how they will revise the Tzismce clan myself and how they will rework Protean in there clan spread. I'm also curious how they will update the Ravnos clan in the current setting and what ligering effects the Week of Nightmares have had on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  More thoughts. 02-08-2023, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T16:11:15-08:00","id":1502546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502527#post1502527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious myself on how they will revise the Tzismce clan myself and how they will rework Protean in there clan spread. I'm also curious how they will update the Ravnos clan in the current setting and what ligering effects the Week of Nightmares have had on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that the Tzimisce write-up is identical to the free revision they already released.<br /> <br /> Ditto the Salubri and Ravnos.<br /> <br /> I mean, why do free write-ups if it's not canon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T18:07:46-08:00","id":1502560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502546#post1502546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that the Tzimisce write-up is identical to the free revision they already released.<br /> <br /> Ditto the Salubri and Ravnos.<br /> <br /> I mean, why do free write-ups if it's not canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, given the way Renegade/Paradox/whoever the current team that does these things has shown in a few books by now how they treat layout and page content, any page that is straight up identical to a previous working makes for multiple pages of an already pricey book with a repeat of material people already have. By which I mean, every page of this thing that repeats something that already exists is that much less space, and not in a small way, for anything new to justify its existence and cost with.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be so bad if the layout was better/there was more content per page/there were more pages per book/the price was something else, or that I didn't expect a bunch of this book to be empty spaces, repeated internal artwork of its cover, big ol larp pictures taking up most of if not an entire page, and so forth, but there's no reason not to expect that at this point. So that being the case, they can at least put some effort and variety into such writing/rules stuff as the book is going to contain.<br /> <br /> At the very least they can throw in some options for said clans to go alongside the existing ones (alternate banes, etc). Even just that would be something as far as at least having been previously vaguely promised and at least hopefully implied by the promo copy (hopefully).<br /> <br /> The idea of instead flat reprint wouldn't bother me so much or even at all in other circumstances. It is legitimately a really good thing to collect all 7 of these clans in one book instead of making people buy two+ whole other books in addition to the core, but the massive overpowering counterweight of that is having seen at this point how these books actually look upon being published, without a whole lot to suggest that is going to change in the future. The material is barely there, and anything they get to just copy and paste more or less makes it even more scant.<br /> <br /> Also there is the inescapable underlying note of &quot;it has been 5 years of this gameline now of it all, but hey, you finally get a player's guide.&quot; A player's guide with a bunch of clans would have been amazing a couple of years in. But this long into this edition? For all that the rolling, repeated marketing theme of WoD5e is that it is mostly targeting people coming into tabletop right this very second and everyone before that second has ceased to have relevance, I'd still like to think enough consideration exists for whatever people have been buying this stuff from the 2018 jump for the past 5 years that they can give them a book that will not simply blow already thin page space just regurgitating things they very likely already have. Listen, I get it, the previous fanbase is a &quot;legacy&quot; fanbase of a &quot;legacy&quot; edition, with all the shrugging brush off that language implies, hey sure, fine, no country for old men. At least work to give this ersatz-replacement fanbase fresh stuff they can use, or really even simply a useful spin on pre existing stuff (whether optional or not), these people have existed for more than a few years now.<br /> <br /> That or do better with use of written content page count vs art choices and empty space on a page, but that's pretty much asking for miracles at this point.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, at this stage of things, it would be something if there was at least some variation of some kind, in some way. This is not a company that has otherwise built up a lot of faith in the idea that they won't do as little as the book allows for doing within its page count, layout and price point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 02-08-2023, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T00:59:19-08:00","id":1502593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502546#post1502546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that the Tzimisce write-up is identical to the free revision they already released.<br /> <br /> Ditto the Salubri and Ravnos.<br /> <br /> I mean, why do free write-ups if it's not canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>They always struck me as an &quot;it'll do.&quot; Option. The tzmisce seemed to have lost a lot of their nuances and esoteric aspects in transition. I think they have the same issue as the lasombra as they don't really thematically mesh with v5.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is obviously trickier and I can't blame them for struggling. The salubri clan flaw wasnt very good and they should have adapted the old one.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT-i know they're not going go do it but re implementing unique disciplines would be a really good idea in this book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-09-2023, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T08:48:35-08:00","id":1502606,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I think Renegade isn't doing nearly as nuanced a job as OPP so my opinion is to keep one's expectations reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T11:22:43-08:00","id":1502617,"title":"","content":"I also hope we get the old clan views on each other again in the new book. It added a little extra flavor to the setting on how varied the clans could be and it was a neat little addition. Speaking of which did any of you ever write down what your character views the other clans for fun. I.E.<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;They are called the Learned Clan, but with a few exceptions I have yet to see it and they come across as mindless brutes who want to create a failed experiment over and over again and we are called the mad ones.&quot; by an unnamed Malkavian<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-09-2023, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T11:44:39-08:00","id":1502620,"title":"","content":"We've had confirmation so far by both Martyna and Matt Holland that we should be getting updated clan writeups (probably verbs-aligned, though, so not everyone's cup of tea), alternate Banes and new Discipline and Sorcery powers (the teaser says 40, so it should be a sizable expansion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T12:04:00-08:00","id":1502622,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in the January 2023 update video Outstar did talk about these being new writeups. So it isn't a copy-paste-job. As to how different they are, who knows... The way Outstar talked about is that it was done with the goal to bring more clarity. And she did say her favorite was the new write-up for the Banu Haquim which gave a more accessible presentation to the Clan in describing what the Clan is about. That's her take on it at least.<br /> <br /> The deep dive from Renegade-Con mentioned that the book would have more than 200 pages (but the guy didn't remember the exact number but it's in that ballpark).<br /> <br /> Also what hasn't been mentioned in this thread yet from the Deep Dive: The book will have character-creation rules for mortals and ghouls (called &quot;castoffs&quot;). And it will talk about options for character-creation like what if you only want to do a oneshot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T05:57:39-08:00","id":1502744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502622#post1502622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in the January 2023 update video Outstar did talk about these being new writeups. So it isn't a copy-paste-job. As to how different they are, who knows... The way Outstar talked about is that it was done with the goal to bring more clarity. And she did say her favorite was the new write-up for the Banu Haquim which gave a more accessible presentation to the Clan in describing what the Clan is about. That's her take on it at least.<br /> <br /> The deep dive from Renegade-Con mentioned that the book would have more than 200 pages (but the guy didn't remember the exact number but it's in that ballpark).<br /> <br /> Also what hasn't been mentioned in this thread yet from the Deep Dive: The book will have character-creation rules for mortals and ghouls (called &quot;castoffs&quot;). And it will talk about options for character-creation like what if you only want to do a oneshot.</div> </div> </div> </div>They confirmed 256 pages in the chat on the stream.<br /> <br /> Here's everything in detail on the two upcoming V5 books, from the stream (I haven't gone through WoD news and added to this, will probably do that later today):<br /> <br /> Summary from the stream for the Player's Guide...Conceptually the PG is a main companion to the core book, giving you two books to comprehensively cover most things you'll need at the table with most of your player options<ul><li>Will have the 7 core clans and all the clans from the other books all compiled. When asked about copy/paste, it was mentioned the core clans would be presented with a fresh perspective so it's not just a cut-and-paste job</li> <li>Will have variant clan banes and advice for how to use the variant banes, which can be applied to individual characters or a whole clan</li> <li>Disciplines have a whole set of new options, as well as copying/compiling Disciplines from the other books such as Oblivion. Example: Animalism focusing on interaction with animals (they talked about many animalism powers focusing on the Beast already, so swinging the other way), mention of some new BS rituals</li> <li>Whole chapter expanding on playing 'cast offs' such as Caitiff, Duskborn, ghouls and mortals. New TB Merits and Flaws, clarifications on TBA access</li> <li>Confirmed page count of 256</li> <li>Repeats and clarifications for creating your own characters. Quick ways to 'get into' building character for things like one shots.</li> <li>Collected Predator Types and added a few new PTs, mentioned trapdoor spider-style or stalker style without 'naming' them</li> <li>Coterie tracking sheet will be provided. Collecting the clan coterie merits from companion and adding to them for things such as TBs (mentioned something about an immortal heart merit to remind others about humanity, caitiff with versatile blood and salubri sharing their restraint with others).</li> <li>Advice on personalizing chronicles. Additional options for playstyles, sample slates of personal convictions to go with some character concepts/inspire them. Also some advice for using Touchstones, what happens when Touchstones become aware of kindred society, gaining new touchstones, characters with no touchstones keeping them tied to the mortal world. Specifically no objects as touchstones.</li> <li>Simplified rules for Projects, some new rules for Memoriams. Expanded considerate play/advice for dealing with sensitive topics.</li> <li>PDF is 'safe bet' to see early, especially with preorder</li> </ul>More Player's Guide info from the WoD News...<ul><li>Revisits all aspects of character and coterie creation. Includes streamlined guidance for new and experienced players, including an 'instant vampire' section.</li> <li>Collects all the Discipline powers from non-core sourcebooks except for a few that need the excess material from the book they came from or were plot device-ish (example: Ex Nihilo and its need for the deep explanations of the underworld from Cults).</li> <li>40 new Discipline powers, powers for all of the clans. There will be some clarifications and errata such as different rolls to existing Disciplines as well.</li> <li>Won't be reprinting powers from the Sabbat book (as this is a player facing guide, no need to reprint antagonist powers)</li> <li>New Predator Types including Grim Reaper, Montero, Pursuer and Trapdoor. No other context given. Leaving out Roadside Killer in the Predator Type compilation.</li> <li>New Coterie Merits, Flaws, Clan Coterie Merits and Coterie Domain Traits.</li> <li>The guidelines for non-traditional chronicles include things such as all-thin blood, troupe, streaming/online play, chronicles without a storyteller, other styles of play.</li> <li>No Loresheets in PG\u200b - EDIT: It was confirmed the Bloodline loresheets from Cults will be reprinted</li> </ul><br /> Not a lot on Blood Sigils, they said there'll be more in the March 1st stream. From the stream for Blood Sigils (more to come in March per the stream)...<ul><li>Narratively, different types of blood magic are becoming available to lots of types of Kindred due to recent changes, which drives a lot of what's in the book.</li> <li>Not just a book about BS and TBA dots, but also helps integrating them into the story.</li> <li>Will have some 'weird stuff in the book' when asked the question about artifacts/things created by sorcerers (not confirmed to what degree, both to not spoil as well as in case anything gets cut)</li> <li>A sample story outline/sketch in the book with examples of how characters can get drawn into the underground blood magic scene in a given city and things like trading rituals or 'mercenary' use of the BS/TBA</li> <li>Can just take the book for more cool powers, but there's a lot more in it than that</li> <li>More information on the March 1st stream</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 02-15-2023, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T06:57:06-08:00","id":1502746,"title":"","content":"No loresheets in the PG? That's a shame, that, the Clan writeups, and Oblivion are pretty much the only reasons I was waiting for the PG, and half of that is because I'm not personally interested in CbN or CotBG (I know they're meant to be really good, In fact they're one of the few things V5 has over Requiem and V20.<br /> <br /> After this and the W5 debarkle it might be time for me to just drop WoD entirely for CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T10:02:13-08:00","id":1502762,"title":"","content":"That's cool that there is more predator types and coterie boons to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T05:37:19-08:00","id":1502828,"title":"","content":"I remember a time - a simple time - when all the clans were in one book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:40:05-08:00","id":1502856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502746#post1502746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No loresheets in the PG? That's a shame,</div> </div> </div> </div>In this regard, Justin Achilli really complicated matters, though, didn't he? V5 for all its changes still portrayed itself as a continuation of old VtM lore and as being part of that same narrative universe. But with W5 JA led with the explicit statement that W5 would not be a continuation and that 90% of the old lore from previous editions wouldn't be canon anymore. So, now what? Do you take that approach with all WOD5E stuff from now on...? Do you make V5 an exception?<br /> <br /> Of course, Justin Achilli's already gone... So he created W5 with a very different premise than V5 althoug both should be part of WOD5E - and then he left.<br /> <br /> There are supposedly loresheets in W5 but who knows what they're like and it certainly could've been the case that the V5 players guide was written when it wasn't even clear yet what W5 loresheets would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T11:30:20-08:00","id":1502859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502828#post1502828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember a time - a simple time - when all the clans were in one book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, aside from V20 that's never been the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T12:04:04-08:00","id":1502862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502859#post1502859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, aside from V20 that's never been the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised did it as well.<br /> <br /> Edit- and both dark age and victorian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-12-2023, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T12:11:51-08:00","id":1502863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502862#post1502862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised did it as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>As did V:tDA and DA:V. Even Victorian Age supplement, while not a core book, featured them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T15:01:48-08:00","id":1502880,"title":"","content":"Literally since the Dark Ages released in 1996 they've included all Clans. But naaaaaahhhhh, it's cool waiting five years for all 13 to get a splat in 2023 instead of, you know, in the same core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T22:53:58-08:00","id":1502913,"title":"","content":"Its understandable that v5 didn't have the other 7 clans in the corebook (although the thinbloods do implicitly undermine this). The game did reinvent the wheel to a degree, but it is a little excessive that they where then released in a fragmented piecemeal way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T03:28:19-08:00","id":1502920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502913#post1502913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its understandable that v5 didn't have the other 7 clans in the corebook (although the thinbloods do implicitly undermine this). The game did reinvent the wheel to a degree, but it is a little excessive that they where then released in a fragmented piecemeal way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lack of a good editor and a generally poor approach to editing and layout of that book meant something needed to be cut. And considering how much these games are about a experience focused on No Sabbat-Camarilla Bad-Anarchs Good it made sense to cut the weird clans from the core. It's just a subpar offering for those of us playing from the second half of 90s being used to that being in every book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T05:31:42-08:00","id":1502921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502920#post1502920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And considering how much these games are about a experience focused on No Sabbat-Camarilla Bad-Anarchs Good it made sense to cut the weird clans from the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the Harry Potter Tier political metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T07:45:00-08:00","id":1502929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502920#post1502920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the lack of a good editor and a generally poor approach to editing and layout of that book meant something needed to be cut. And considering how much these games are about a experience focused on No Sabbat-Camarilla Bad-Anarchs Good it made sense to cut the weird clans from the core. It's just a subpar offering for those of us playing from the second half of 90s being used to that being in every book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I suspect that martins white wolf would have eventually released all class relatively promptly considering anarch and carmarilla got two out relatively. The 'incident' obviously hobbled development to degree. On reflection they were putting the cart before the horse.<br /> <br /> I mean the thinbloods and caitiff as written should have been the first thing edited out and saved for anarch. This would have freed up a lot of space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T11:17:33-08:00","id":1502940,"title":"","content":"Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T11:35:25-08:00","id":1502943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502940#post1502940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're supposed to be the ultimate Outcasts, and as such are deeply aspirational for the thematic undertone of the current version of Vampire. I've not seen much interest in people playing them over the decades, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T11:55:39-08:00","id":1502946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502940#post1502940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of course only for my group and from a non-V5 perspective (yet) since we are waiting for the players guide for easy access to non-corebook clans:<br /> <br /> No not at all. That flavor of underdog-fantasy never appealed to any of my players. Unlikely to change even with the new thin-blood mechanics in V5. They like to dive deep into clan culture.<br /> <br /> I had one request for a caitiff character concept, but that was only because a new player wanted a child vampire with protean AND dementation. Yeah...that did not happen ^^'<br /> <br /> That said there are some interesting caitiff chars in the meta-plot imho e.g. Mukhtar Bey from Cairo by Night. Hope he comes up again someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T12:17:09-08:00","id":1502949,"title":"","content":"People playing Panders is extraordinarily rare in my experience, and I have yet to have one person play a thinblood. People want to play VAMPIRES. Full on, honest to god, VAMPIRES. They want to do the cool stuff they see in movies. Full powers, even the full weakness experience of dodging sunbeams Near Dark style during a daylight attack. If someone is playing a Gangrel, they want the full experience of turning into the friggin Wolfman during a frenzy. If someone is playing a Toreador, they want the full experience of sipping blood from wineglasses at lavish parties, and angsting about how the ugliness of the world is literally poisoning them. They want to play VAMPIRES, not cursed humans seeking to kill the REAL vampires and thereby cure themselves.<br /> <br /> They don't want to burn down the castle. They want to OWN the castle, which is why playing the guys trying to burn down the castle has never been remotely as attractive as the creators of the game want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T13:17:28-08:00","id":1502953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502940#post1502940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> caitiff/pandera are pretty common, I tend to see them at the same rate as most clans generally, ive played one. The Sabbat game I'm in the pander is currently worried what will happen when someone find out someone taught her obtenerbration....<br /> <br /> I've seen in 15 years one thinblood and thats when their powers where more varied than diet thaumaturgy. People don't tend to play them because it's just a caitiff except harder to integrate and less useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-14-2023, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T13:42:02-08:00","id":1502954,"title":"","content":"I have a pretty large group of newbie gamers, they are 10 aged between 15 and 30, with an average of 6 attending. We have two Thin Bloods, one chose them because she wanted to climb Kindred society the hard way, the other because she liked the idea of treading the balance between her mortal life and vampiric society.<br /> <br /> We also have a number of them at our V5 Larp, 3 Thin Bloods and 2 Ghouls out of 30 players. Thin Blood Alchemy is well liked.<br /> <br /> Caitiff are not popular instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-13-2023, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T14:17:17-08:00","id":1502956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502940#post1502940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> Caitiff, on their own, don't really appeal. I don't dislike them and I'm not drawn to them, they're just there. My players share the sentiment, they're too busy deciding what clan to play to even look at them. Nobody's against playing with one of the thinblood flaws in theory, it just hasn't happened so far.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm particularly encouraging it. I used to have a fondness for the thinbloods, though as regular vampires who happen to have low generation, not as their mangled &quot;duskborn semi-clan&quot; stuff in V5. Fifth editions attitude towards them is beginning to rub me the wrong way for reasons I can't quite put my finger on and it's leaving a bad taste in my mouth when I think about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T14:18:30-08:00","id":1502957,"title":"","content":"Ah, out of the 3 convention games I usually run (thrice a year on average), two have full Thin Blood coteries: one is a conspiracy of anarchists, the other one a rock band, trying to adjust to Kindred politics and to the temptation of Diablerie respectively.<br /> <br /> So far, we've always had positive feedback on the games involving them (in one case, we've directly caused the acquisition of two V5 corebooks from the nearby shop!).<br /> <br /> Of course, they are games me and two other Storytellers of our association have created, so the sample is self-selected, but we've found Thin Bloods to be quite useful for convention games: they are easy to explain, easy to learn, easy to build and very customizable.<br /> \u200b<br /> (the third game is a bit more over the top and is set in the Dark Ages, with a group of ancillae Tzimisce knights choosing between their Convictions and their feudal obligations. I've been working on a fourth game, set in the Salt Lake City Tremere chantry during the Fall of the Pyramid, but I'm still not happy with the structure)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T20:08:10-08:00","id":1502992,"title":"","content":"Caitiff, as far as I understand have three loose purposes: to be the lowest rank of kindred society, to be a catch-all for concepts that don't fit the Clans, and to be a sign of Gehenna as whatever caused Clans in the first place slowly fades. Unfortunately the first makes them unappealing to play, it turns out that six of the seven core clans are broad enough for the second to rarely matter (especially after another six Clans and dozen Bloodlines), and the third is entirely a plot-based thing. Thin-Bloods also served points one and three to an even greater degree, and tended to be Caitiff anyway, which makes them even less desirable.<br /> <br /> Then we get into the simple fact that a lot of people don't want to be playing struggling neonates, they want to play the politics of ancillae or elders. Which makes the social exclusion that perfectly primes Caitiff for a Starving Anarchs games serve as an active detriment worse than being an extremist Brujah demagogue (who, thanks to their Clan, at least had a seat at the table until V5).<br /> <br /> It's not really a surprise Requiem combined both into Revenants and implied that they shouldn't be a player option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 02-15-2023, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T01:39:14-08:00","id":1503007,"title":"","content":"I like Caitiff, but I also really like clans. When I make a Caitiff character, the goal is usually the same as other characters: I want to get my own territory and accumulate backgrounds, make friends, undermine enemies and so on. Immediately B-lining towards freedom fighter is foolish. Caitiff are great for versatile characters, IE you want to get 3 or more dots in more than 3 disciplines, or when you want the disciplines near one clan but don't think the weakness matches the concept you have. Being the subject of discrimination is something you can mitigate if you're clever, and it's not like the Caitiff are the only subject of vampire discrimination.<br /> <br /> Thinbloods though? Your only goal is to become a real vampire. You might as well be playing a Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T02:05:27-08:00","id":1503009,"title":"","content":"Caitiff work as the &quot;ordinary person.&quot; Or &quot;I didn't choose to be a vampire&quot; Vampire. You can fit them in elsewhere but it's a good angle to play. Theirs also a lot of angles that can be unique points: discrimination, disenfranchisement, low cultural capital, discipline layout, who exactly is your sire etc. Lots of interesting ingredients for the pot.<br /> <br /> To give an example by last caitiff was a stray shovelhead who was saved by a tremere (a pc from another game) who recognised her as a person she knew (they were both in uni) she's the childer of an established Sabbat priest whose (also a pc) from another game. Her main discipline lineup is auspex, obfuscate, fortitude and Dominate which comes from mentorship by the tremere and living rough and her ultimate descent from malkavians. Her real gift is her tech skills and talent for larceny. She tended to cover a lot of logistical and unglamorous work in the anarchs (tremere had her smuggled to anarch domains) often cleaning up masquarade breaches and logistics.<br /> <br /> Nothing about this pc couldn't fit into another clan but her caitiff status synergises very well here.<br /> <br /> Thin bloods issue issue is their fulfill the same niche in game caitiff but mechanically they're clunky an awkward. Caitiff are effectively the same as clan vampires when push comes to shove but thin bloods operate under seperate mechanics, ecology and power level. It's like running a sorceror in a masters game vs running a craft mage in a tradition one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T10:17:06-08:00","id":1503041,"title":"","content":"Outstar talked about the V5 players guide <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VUipVVycyQg\" target=\"_blank\">last week</a> and here's some extra information she offered there:<ul><li>It was in development for a long time and there were a couple different iterations of the book</li> <li>This time she called the Clans-sections and Discipline-sections a \u201creprint\u201d</li> <li>But she also mentioned that some powers that were in the past books won\u2019t be in the Players Guide if they require too much explanation</li> <li>Example: The Oblivion-ritual \u201cEx Nihilo\u201d which allows vampires to go to the Shadowlands and the authors decided this required too much extra information</li> <li>They also added 40 new powers, though, as a trade-off</li> <li>No Disciplines that were found in the Sabbat Book either because it\u2019s a Players Guide</li> <li>Collects all the Predator-types from the past sourcebooks plus four new ones</li> <li>Roadkiller-Predator-type won\u2019t be included, though</li> <li>The new ones are \u201cGrim Reaper\u201d, \u201cPursuer\u201d and \u201cTrapdoor\u201d (the fourth one I didn\u2019t really understand, something like \u201cMontaro\u201d)</li> <li>Coterie-rules include Clan/Thinblood-Coterie Merits, Flaws, Coterie-Domain-rules and with an extra sheet to be used</li> <li>New Merits and Flaws, including ones for Caitiff, Thinbloods, Mortals and Ghouls</li> <li>One additional alternative Bane for each Clan</li> <li>There\u2019s a revised approach for Touchstones, Memoriam and projects in the game</li> <li>There are some clarifications for how some Disciplines work and what rolls are associated with certain Discipline-powers are sometimes being revised in the Players Guide</li> </ul><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T11:35:46-08:00","id":1503047,"title":"","content":"What's the Road killer predator type? Run people over and drink from them while their down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:07:12-08:00","id":1503050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503047#post1503047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the Road killer predator type? Run people over and drink from them while their down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mentioned in the chronicle book Let The Streets Run Red:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Predator Type: Roadside Killer<br /> You belong with the vagabonds, tourists, and truckers of the world \u2014 always moving, never at home. You know how to pick out the ones whose deaths are discounted as the risk of a woman hitchhiking alone, or who simply won\u2019t be missed at all. You still have to fight to keep other vampires away from them lest the herd thins too much, though.<br /> <br /> In life, you either were one of them, or you met these vagrants as they rested at your roadside stop.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T14:58:13-08:00","id":1503068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503050#post1503050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was mentioned in the chronicle book Let The Streets Run Red:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Can I ask what the skill, asset, and discipline spread is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T16:20:10-08:00","id":1503079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503068#post1503068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Can I ask what the skill, asset, and discipline spread is?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Add a specialty Survival (the road) or Investigation (vampire cant)</li> <li>Add one dot of Fortitude or Protean</li> <li>Gain two additional dots of migrating Herd</li> <li>Gain the Flaw Prey Exclusion (locals)</li> </ul>Predator Pool: Dexterity or Charisma + Drive, you feed by picking up down and outs with nowhere else to go.\u200b </div> </div> </div>What I forgot to add: The reason why this one won't be part of the Players Guide according to Outstar is that 1) not many people in the community used that Predator type and 2) it was already kinda covered by Alleycat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:31:41-08:00","id":1503087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503079#post1503079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What I forgot to add: The reason why this one won't be part of the Players Guide according to Outstar is that 1) not many people in the community used that Predator type and 2) it was already kinda covered by Alleycat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T15:41:31-08:00","id":1503175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502856#post1502856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this regard, Justin Achilli really complicated matters, though, didn't he? V5 for all its changes still portrayed itself as a continuation of old VtM lore and as being part of that same narrative universe. But with W5 JA led with the explicit statement that W5 would not be a continuation and that 90% of the old lore from previous editions wouldn't be canon anymore. So, now what? Do you take that approach with all WOD5E stuff from now on...? Do you make V5 an exception?<br /> <br /> Of course, Justin Achilli's already gone... So he created W5 with a very different premise than V5 althoug both should be part of WOD5E - and then he left.<br /> <br /> There are supposedly loresheets in W5 but who knows what they're like and it certainly could've been the case that the V5 players guide was written when it wasn't even clear yet what W5 loresheets would be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't lay all that blame on Achilli though. We've been told that most decisions, like the antagonist-focused Sabbat or not worrying about legacy/metaplot dragging forward are PDX macro-level decisions. He's doing the things that Paradox has said they want/need for the line to support its transmedia property goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:09:16-08:00","id":1503179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503175#post1503175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't lay all that blame on Achilli though. We've been told that most decisions, like the antagonist-focused Sabbat or not worrying about legacy/metaplot dragging forward are PDX macro-level decisions. He's doing the things that Paradox has said they want/need for the line to support its transmedia property goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the evidence for that is... what? There are <i>plenty </i>of Justin Achilli's tweets supporting what I stated originally.<br /> <br /> What you're alleging is a conspiracy where Justin Achilli has been pressured into making certain creative decisions.<br /> <br /> After all, there are tweets and dev-blog.posts by Justin Achilli which I have based my comments on. And the only way I could see someone counter such a claim is that someone else made those tweets or those tweets were made under duress. So unless you want to claim something like that happened, I don't know why you would excuse Justin Achilli in his role as &quot;Creative Lead&quot;... unless you also want to argue that the position of &quot;Creative Lead&quot; was meaningless and/or powerless...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:08:04-08:00","id":1503189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503179#post1503179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the evidence for that is... what? There are <i>plenty </i>of Justin Achilli's tweets supporting what I stated originally.<br /> <br /> What you're alleging is a conspiracy where Justin Achilli has been pressured into making certain creative decisions.<br /> <br /> After all, there are tweets and dev-blog.posts by Justin Achilli which I have based my comments on. And the only way I could see someone counter such a claim is that someone else made those tweets or those tweets were made under duress. So unless you want to claim something like that happened, I don't know why you would excuse Justin Achilli in his role as &quot;Creative Lead&quot;... unless you also want to argue that the position of &quot;Creative Lead&quot; was meaningless and/or powerless...</div> </div> </div> </div>I love how you jump right to 'oh god conspiracy'. It's not. It's just a statement from Outstar, on one of the Discords, when asked about the state of the World of Darkness. Here's the quote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Outstar from Discord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We gave an interview to VentureBeat about a year ago that goes in detail into that subject, and I would say it didn\u2019t age badly at all! Please check it out here: <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/for-world-of-darkness-the-future-of-tabletop-rpgs-is-increasingly-digital/\" target=\"_blank\">https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/f...ingly-digital/</a><br /> <br /> The keywords are \u201cmedia-agnostic\u201d and \u201ctransmedia\u201d. Since then, we\u2019ve announced our Hollywood-adjacent partnership and plans of bringing WoD to small and big screens, which also explains it further. Our stories need to work at the TTRPG table just like they need to work in a video game, comic book, actual play, immersive experience or on the silver screen - and our approach to IP development treats this as a baseline. TTRPG corebooks become guides for our partners on how to work with our IPs, and when we write these materials, we keep this firmly in mind.<br /> <br /> To give a live example - explanations on how antagonists in V5 Sabbat behave in detail, what sounds or gestures they would make - this is super helpful for storytellers at the tables, but also it would help TV writers nail this down in a script, or video game designers develop them well for in-game worlds.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That, combined with other statements about the IP from other WoD team about accessibility and not having to worry about lore or old material (such as the way the V5 wiki is sourced, ignoring things that aren't in a V5 book, for example), and mentions about not needing to worry about lore as tweets and statement from other WoD employees, and the way the books haven't worried about dragging lore forward under PDX's direct involvement, paints a pretty clear picture.<br /> <br /> A creative lead still has to adhere to any mandates the IP owners have, and Achilli would obviously be working within the bounds that Paradox has set. He's responsible for some, sure, but probably not literally everything that people lay at his feet or literally every decision made about the line. Because on a macro level, he's not in charge of the direction and needs of the IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:09:06-08:00","id":1503190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503079#post1503079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) not many people in the community used that Predator type</div> </div> </div> </div>So they say after publishing it in <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:18:00-08:00","id":1503192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503190#post1503190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they say after publishing it in <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know... It begs the question: &quot;based on what metric...?&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, if you're just gonna do a summary of all the player-options presented in various books that were presented before, why be selective now...?<br /> <br /> It was okay before but now it isn't good enough for the Players Guide...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T19:08:25-08:00","id":1503199,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's fully possible that JA was told to make W5 and H5 break away from old lore and everything and had no issue with it, or even agreed with it. It certainly seems to agree with what he wanted nWoD to be two decades ago. It's possible that he even went further than he was told to, unless somebody gains access to WW documents or conversations regarding this stuff.<br /> <br /> I'll note that Vampire is the one where they're most likely to want to cling to old lore, due to it being the line with the most mainstream presence from Kindred: the Embraced and Bloodlines (particularly Bloodlines). Hence why it got the soft reboot back to a pseudo-1e status with hints of Bloodlines, whereas H5 and W5 got full reboots (the former so bad that my version of VtM now has the Malleus Maleficarum instead of the SoL). With V5 they wanted to use the more mainstream bits to draw people in, whereas Apocalypse and Reckoning are obscure enough to get as thoroughly cleansed of the right wing elements as possible (despite such elements being satire).<br /> <br /> After you've done that Justin's job becomes clear: when you've taken away 90% of a game you've got to find <b>something</b> to put in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T19:34:53-08:00","id":1503202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503199#post1503199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's fully possible that JA was told to make W5 and H5 break away from old lore and everything and had no issue with it, or even agreed with it. It certainly seems to agree with what he wanted nWoD to be two decades ago. It's possible that he even went further than he was told to, unless somebody gains access to WW documents or conversations regarding this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have official stuff like dev-blogs and tweets from people like Justin Achilli... and anything beyond that is speculation sadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503199#post1503199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note that Vampire is the one where they're most likely to want to cling to old lore, due to it being the line with the most mainstream presence from Kindred: the Embraced and Bloodlines (particularly Bloodlines). Hence why it got the soft reboot back to a pseudo-1e status with hints of Bloodlines, whereas H5 and W5 got full reboots (the former so bad that my version of VtM now has the Malleus Maleficarum instead of the SoL). With V5 they wanted to use the more mainstream bits to draw people in, whereas Apocalypse and Reckoning are obscure enough to get as thoroughly cleansed of the right wing elements as possible (despite such elements being satire).<br /> <br /> After you've done that Justin's job becomes clear: when you've taken away 90% of a game you've got to find <b>something</b> to put in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean this description misconstrues what happened... It isn't like Justin Achilli had been in charge from the start... So what WOD5E started out as with the release of the V5 corebook under the direction of Martin Ericsson was different from what Justin Achilli wanted to do with WOD5E.<br /> <br /> So of course V5 is different from H5 and W5. It has less to do with the nature of the games and more to do with the change in lead-personnel.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli's very different vision of WOD5E was announced with his W5-dev-blogpost last year by announcing that W5 wouldn't be a continuation of old WtA-editions and that it would it be safe to assume that anything from the old editions wouldn't be canon anymore.<br /> <br /> So the reboots for H5 and W5 were Justin Achilli's decisions while the person responsible for V5's different treatment in that regard was Martin Ericsson.<br /> <br /> And we all know why the switch in personnel happened... so let's not pretend there's some sort of smooth continuity between V5 at the start and what became of WOD5E these days with H5 and W5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T05:22:23-08:00","id":1503227,"title":"","content":"It could be both. Paradox's decisions might be aligned with justins outlook. It's a nice idea that Paradox is cracking a wip on his back as he guts settings or oblivious suits not paying attention to justin trying to make cofd 3.0 but the truth is probably more complex","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T07:06:35-08:00","id":1503237,"title":"","content":"From everything we've seen, both Ericsson and Justin had free reign as it doesn't seem to me like Paradox understands RPG's very well. They did have probably strategic goals, but in general they let them do what they wanted until it blew up in their face or they left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T08:27:02-08:00","id":1503240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503237#post1503237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From everything we've seen, both Ericsson and Justin had free reign as it doesn't seem to me like Paradox understands RPG's very well. They did have probably strategic goals, but in general they let them do what they wanted until it blew up in their face or they left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do lean towards that interpretation, v5's attitude to combat vs blood hunt shows a massive disconnect between the two groups outlook. But it is plausable that Paradox are well aware of justins actions but percieve it as beneficial to their objections. Weither this is a massive error would be another issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T09:07:53-08:00","id":1503242,"title":"","content":"I don't think Justin was removed or missed some goal of Paradox. They seemed pretty aligned with him and happ with him as a spokeperson. He just got a better job offer and took it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T10:48:27-08:00","id":1503249,"title":"","content":"I agree, it's definitely compatible goals - both he and Paradox wanted something accessible to new players and streamlined from the build-up of contingent material you get from multiple editions and dozens of supplements over the years. Very much a cut-down version of Vampire. Legacy edition fanbase was not the core target audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:14:08-08:00","id":1503273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503242#post1503242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Justin was removed or missed some goal of Paradox. They seemed pretty aligned with him and happ with him as a spokeperson. He just got a better job offer and took it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He left because he couldn't/wouldn't move his family to Sweden, from what was said elsewhere. He was working as just a contractor for a while before he left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:21:44-08:00","id":1503274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503273#post1503273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He left because he couldn't/wouldn't move his family to Sweden, from what was said elsewhere. He was working as just a contractor for a while before he left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would he have to move to Sweden? Renegade is mostly American, Paradox is an international corporation and he can coordinate freelancers and contractors from anywhere in the world. Do you have a citation for that?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:42:06-08:00","id":1503283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1502940#post1502940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know anyone that uses Catiffs and thin-bloods at all in there games? We just reference them sometimes in our game and not much else is done with them and we prefer to use the clans the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>the game i've been running for over a year has been entirely thinbloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T23:41:20-08:00","id":1503358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503283#post1503283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the game i've been running for over a year has been entirely thinbloods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That could work since it avoids the awkward dynamics. I'd be tempted to implement a seperate powers line in outside of poor man's thaumaturgy in such a game. On reflection I'd give them the v5 disciplines and have the vampires swinging v20 tier powers around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:30:45-08:00","id":1503385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503237#post1503237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From everything we've seen, both Ericsson and Justin had free reign as it doesn't seem to me like Paradox understands RPG's very well. They did have probably strategic goals, but in general they let them do what they wanted until it blew up in their face or they left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Role-playing computer games in general do tend to need the most planning and a careful approach during development, implementation, and after release also as well in regard to expansion packs, patches, DLCs, and updates.<br /> All the varied and different gameplay mechanics and systems have to interact for a positive, reasonable, nice, and complex experience, trials, ordeals, and adventure. The various needed and noteworthy systems are numerous: the character creation, protagonist development, choices and decisions during the story, consistency of themes and narration, resolutions at finale, philosophy and morality, balance and fairness both in combat and during other interactions (be it trade, crafting, or diplomacy), travelling and as well upkeep mechanics and choices.<br /> <br /> Which might be why some cRPG games were put on hold, delayed, or received updates and expansion packs relatively late. I certainly hope that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade Bloodlines 2 </i>will be released, upgraded, and updated without troublesome situations and problematic issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T15:39:50-08:00","id":1503404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503237#post1503237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From everything we've seen, both Ericsson and Justin had free reign as it doesn't seem to me like Paradox understands RPG's very well. They did have probably strategic goals, but in general they let them do what they wanted until it blew up in their face or they left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that. Especially because of how Justin Achilli's approach to W5 ignored the idea of a trans-media-approach. After all, JA deciding to have a W5 that abandons 90% of the old canon and outright saying that W5 wouldn't be a &quot;continuationaion&quot; of old editions means that he actively chose to render already recently released games like Earthblood and Heartsong to be non-canon. How's that for trans-media-sympathy...? Justin Achilli chose to abandon the idea of WOD5E as a trans-media-property because he wanted WOD5E to be totally separate from the old canon. At least, that's what he did with W5... but of course he's already gone (even before W5 got released).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T16:08:30-08:00","id":1503406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503404#post1503404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with that. Especially because of how Justin Achilli's approach to W5 ignored the idea of a trans-media-approach. After all, JA deciding to have a W5 that abandons 90% of the old canon and outright saying that W5 wouldn't be a &quot;continuationaion&quot; of old editions means that he actively chose to render already recently released games like Earthblood and Heartsong to be non-canon. How's that for trans-media-sympathy...? Justin Achilli chose to abandon the idea of WOD5E as a trans-media-property because he wanted WOD5E to be totally separate from the old canon. At least, that's what he did with W5... but of course he's already gone (even before W5 got released).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'm pretty sure he ran that up the totem pole. That's a big decision, and one that's related to the percieved baggage of Werewolf. Remember that the conversations and memes about Werewolf are worse than the actual books, and those memes and tweetstorms are easier to handle if you make a clean break and just remove anything that could offend anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T16:40:23-08:00","id":1503407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503406#post1503406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I'm pretty sure he ran that up the totem pole. That's a big decision, and one that's related to the percieved baggage of Werewolf. Remember that the conversations and memes about Werewolf are worse than the actual books, and those memes and tweetstorms are easier to handle if you make a clean break and just remove anything that could offend anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. For JA, abandoning the old lore was the &quot;big revelation&quot; in developing W5. And maybe Paradox felt that this would also be a great approach to avoid anything like the V5 scandal.<br /> <br /> So, the two perspectives aligned in what W5 should be like.<br /> <br /> But it should be made clear that JA was the one with the idea of abandoning the old canon. He wasn't the first person to work on W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T20:46:48-08:00","id":1503422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503249#post1503249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, it's definitely compatible goals - both he and Paradox wanted something accessible to new players and streamlined from the build-up of contingent material you get from multiple editions and dozens of supplements over the years. Very much a cut-down version of Vampire. Legacy edition fanbase was not the core target audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, I just find how Paradox handles this IP, compared to how they handle their grand strategy IP games, to be really funny. <br /> <br /> So, Paradox owns the IP for oWoD right? That means all the sale revenue they might get from old guidebooks, lorebooks, old material in general etc. from throughout the years of White Wolf will go to them, right? By making the new editions have no continuity with the &quot;legacy&quot; material, it will just make new people interested in getting generally immersed in the lore of the franchise.. not get the old material. Now it's all obsolete and there is no point. <br /> <br /> It could be an argument for &quot;accessibility&quot; to bring new people into the franchise (the real success of that is yet to truly be determined.. let's just wait and see how W5 pans out), but Paradox as a company isn't one for a tradition of &quot;accessibility&quot; for getting new people into their franchises.<br /> <br /> Their main strategy as of late (for awhile, actually) is to just make barebone games, then pump them full of DLCs that significantly raises the barrier-of-entry for potentially new players to get an actual quality product. Already established players for their games keep getting the DLCs, because they've already sunk so much money into the product and don't want the feeling of &quot;missing out&quot; on some new key mechanic locked behind DLC.<br /> <br /> I somewhat get why they do what do, because the specific &quot;Non-Turned-Based Real-Time Grand Strategy Map Games&quot; that focuses on alternate history... is a specific and very niche genre. The general market of that, compared to the more normative genres out in the market, have an exceeding difference in size to one another.<br /> <br /> They're trying to mitigate the difference by making their games more casual as of late, but no matter what they'll do (and I don't Paradox will ever understand this), the type games they make will be still niche and it WILL inevitably appeal to compact group of people. It's the reason why Victoria 3 still has mixed reviews months later after its release, because Paradox thinks it can transition to a more casual audience while ignoring the &quot;old&quot; audience (sound familiar?). <br /> <br /> This all rings-around back to oWoD. Tabletop, especially in the modern era, appeals to an even <b>SMALLER</b> set of people compared to video games. Even DnD, the king of Tabletop games has only a moderately-large playerbase. It just has high profitability because DnD players on average are, somewhat wealthy, or <i>very</i> wealthy hobbyists. WotC didn't realize that when they alienated their audience. And look what happened with them?<br /> <br /> oWoD isn't even near the same league as DnD. Paradox can't keep alienating the so-called &quot;legacy fanbase&quot; of oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T10:08:33-08:00","id":1503457,"title":"","content":"Another reason it's not a hot idea to alienate &quot;legacy fans&quot; is that, in reality, you NEED these fans to grow the audience.<br /> <br /> TTRPGs, even at their most rules lite, are complicated games, with necessary knowledge on how to run them effectively that just isn't conveyed in the books themselves. Few people wholly learn D&amp;D, for example, from cracking open the rulebooks and reading them cover to cover. It's both a lot to take in and leaves a great deal out.<br /> <br /> Rather, TTRPGs are as much a folk tradition as products sold by a publisher. Folk traditions that are passed down by experienced players/GMs. These &quot;old fans&quot; are responsible for on-boarding new people and initiating them into the folk tradition. Whether that's an older relative/friend taking the kids aside to play, or content creators putting out videos or podcasts giving lessons and telling &quot;war stories&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would never have started DMing D&amp;D if not for the videos of Matt Colville, for example. And this very forum is a repository of weird and specific knowledge about the World of Darkness that is invaluable for new fans. The &quot;grognards&quot; are hardly infallible and sometimes hew to stagnant play patterns, sure. But there's also deep wells of wisdom to be drawn from. The hand of an &quot;old fan&quot; can sometimes be the difference between a new person being kind of interested in playing, and an actual new player.<br /> <br /> As such, to openly and directly reject established fans is a risky proposition. Grumbling about change aside, old fans generally want their franchise to succeed. If you get them on board, they will proselytize new editions on your behalf. Smoothing over transitions and getting people in the door through word of mouth and institutional knowledge.<br /> <br /> Whereas alienating old fans has the effect of cutting yourself off from that kind of support network. You have to work all the harder to get new people in, and the rulebook must stand all the more on its own. So if the books you're putting out are weak or offer very little, no one is around to pick up the slack and make it work despite itself.<br /> <br /> (All this not touching on if old fans actively <i>hate</i> the new edition, they'll bitterly poison the well against it at every opportunity. Telling new people how much it sucks, and how the old material was so much better. Whether this is &quot;fair&quot; is immaterial; if you alienate the Old Guard, you can't then complain when they turn against you. YOU were the one so confident you could make it without them.)<br /> <br /> Plus, a lot of what people like about an old franchise - what attracts people to it - is often all that &quot;Old Lore&quot;. Throwing it out in the interests of making it &quot;more approachable&quot; can instead nullify one of an established franchise's biggest strengths. It's why DC Comics brought the pre-Flashpoint continuity back after five years of the New 52. And why Games Workshop is reviving their old Warhammer Fantasy setting (the &quot;Old World&quot;) after years of Age of Sigmar. While Old Lore can be daunting, if you just throw it in newbies' faces, it can be a asset too. Sometimes, it's the only part of an old franchise that really appeals to new people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-19-2023, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T10:34:46-08:00","id":1503459,"title":"","content":"I get that, but I think there was a lot of cruft and unnecessary build-up in VtM over the years, and find a good clear-out healthy from time to time when it comes to long-running franchises with contingent variations. V5 has a use-case that V20 doesn't have. If I were to run a game of Vampire with new players, I'd use V5; the system is easier to explain and get running, the basic framework of the setting is easier to explain, and it'd just be a smoother start-up process. If I were to run a game for long-time Vampire fans, I'd probably use V20 instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T11:11:39-08:00","id":1503462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503457#post1503457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason it's not a hot idea to alienate &quot;legacy fans&quot; is that, in reality, you NEED these fans to grow the audience.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Theirs also a product risk of being seen as a company which doesn't respect its fans. How long before they turn on you if they're that contemptuous of people who stuck with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-19-2023, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:04:18-08:00","id":1503469,"title":"","content":"In terms of lore, there's no real meaningful difference between V5 and V20. Sure, there are huge differences. But V5 isn't light on lore to a degree where it's more accessible... Just looking at the Clans, explaining things like the Ministry, Salubri, Hecata or Banu Haquim to new players isn't all that different of a lore-burden compared to the introductions you'd make in a V20 game. Old VtM is intertwined with a ton of lore but it isn't like an encyclopedic knowledge of said lore is a prerequisite for playing V20. The lore-trove of old White Wolf books is what makes the game special. Sure, there needs to be some sort of critical reappraisal of all this writing done in the 90s or early 00s but the dense lore should be viewed as an asset. There aren't many games that have access to something like that.<br /> <br /> And with V5 there was at least still somewhat of an interest to link up the new V5 with the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:26:35-08:00","id":1503477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503469#post1503469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of lore, there's no real meaningful difference between V5 and V20. Sure, there are huge differences. But V5 isn't light on lore to a degree where it's more accessible... Just looking at the Clans, explaining things like the Ministry, Salubri, Hecata or Banu Haquim to new players isn't all that different of a lore-burden compared to the introductions you'd make in a V20 game. Old VtM is intertwined with a ton of lore but it isn't like an encyclopedic knowledge of said lore is a prerequisite for playing V20. The lore-trove of old White Wolf books is what makes the game special. Sure, there needs to be some sort of critical reappraisal of all this writing done in the 90s or early 00s but the dense lore should be viewed as an asset. There aren't many games that have access to something like that.<br /> <br /> And with V5 there was at least still somewhat of an interest to link up the new V5 with the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point. I'm thinking more assessment of the lore - if I tell a new player the Hecata are a group of formerly disparate necromancers who recently unified, they go, okay. If I tell a long-term player that the Hecata exist they're more likely to go, &quot;Wait, that makes no sense! Those groups hated each other!&quot; <br /> <br /> Likewise, if you're expectation is the world-spanning mega conspiracy Camarilla from late VtM 3rd, the desperate underground holding action Camarilla from V5 might throw you off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T13:30:35-08:00","id":1503486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503477#post1503477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fair point. I'm thinking more assessment of the lore - if I tell a new player the Hecata are a group of formerly disparate necromancers who recently unified, they go, okay. If I tell a long-term player that the Hecata exist they're more likely to go, &quot;Wait, that makes no sense! Those groups hated each other!&quot;<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you're expectation is the world-spanning mega conspiracy Camarilla from late VtM 3rd, the desperate underground holding action Camarilla from V5 might throw you off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the classic on I clocked was &quot;why are the anarchs succesful?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T14:38:36-08:00","id":1503492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503274#post1503274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would he have to move to Sweden? Renegade is mostly American, Paradox is an international corporation and he can coordinate freelancers and contractors from anywhere in the world. Do you have a citation for that?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Justin worked for Paradox, not Renegade. With the exception of Jason Karl, who to my knowledge isn't in a creative role, the entire team worked out of Sweden. Based on his tweets he did move there for a time being. When he moved back to the states is when it was announced he was moving to a contract position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T16:37:28-08:00","id":1503500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503492#post1503492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Justin worked for Paradox, not Renegade. With the exception of Jason Karl, who to my knowledge isn't in a creative role, the entire team worked out of Sweden. Based on his tweets he did move there for a time being. When he moved back to the states is when it was announced he was moving to a contract position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and most of the folks he was organising were people in Renegade. I know he was employed by Paradox and I know he moved to and from Sweden for work, but elmerg said that the reason he left was because he couldn't/wouldn't move his family to Sweden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T13:09:11-08:00","id":1503555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503500#post1503500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... but elmerg said that the reason he left was because he couldn't/wouldn't move his family to Sweden.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the reason he gave on Twitter. Then again, the new job may have played a role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T13:19:39-08:00","id":1503557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502380-renegade-publishes-vampire-5e-players-guide?p=1503555#post1503555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the reason he gave on Twitter. Then again, the new job may have played a role.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I was asking for a link, because the only reference I found was during 2021 when the covid restrictions were in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath